# Immich safety

## Gate

Load on every authorized Immich turn (inventory or mutate). Skip when the
turn never touches Immich.

## Read-only default

These are fine without an extra destructive verb when Immich is authorized:

- server-info / health reads
- album / asset / people list and search
- jobs status reads
- asset metadata (not original bytes)

Do **not** delete, create public shares, or change admin users/API keys
unless the user gave an explicit verb **this turn** naming the object(s).

## Mutate gates (explicit verb required)

| Risk | Needs this turn |
| --- | --- |
| Trash / archive | **trash**/**archive** + asset/album ids |
| Permanent delete / empty trash | **delete** + ids |
| Public share link | **share** + scope |
| Album create/update membership | **create**/**update**/**add**/**remove** + ids |
| Admin user / OAuth / API keys | **admin** + named change |

Ambiguous "clean up duplicates" → ask for ids; do not mass-delete.

## Prefer trash

Prefer trash/archive over hard delete when the user only wants items gone
from the library view. Empty-trash is permanent — require an explicit
empty/delete verb.

## Refuse

- Pasting API keys, OAuth secrets, or user passwords into chat
- Dumping original media bytes or EXIF secret material into chat
- Inventing album/asset/person ids
- Absorbing Nextcloud / *arr / Plex into this surface

## Receipt examples (safe)

Inventory turn: album `Wedding` id `…` count 120 — no mutate.

Trash turn (authorized): trashed assets `a1`, `a2` — no keys; originals not
dumped.

